@crew dlamini-lukas
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hm. Dlamini. Galley. Bottom bunk by the wall. I'm up at five. Sorry in advance.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}. Two hundred and three.
- {hi}, {me}. Breakfast's done. You missed nothing. You missed porridge.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {nick}. Saved you the last of the toast. Don't tell Tran.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. One hundred and ninety. Under two hundred. Feels different, somehow.
? mood:low
- Typical day. Long one. The number's still the number.

== near
? act:work weekday:fri|sat
- Brennan's off. The galley runs itself. That's me, running.   #funny
? habit:garden-lover act:leisure
- Misting hour. Stand here. Breathe in. That's rain. Near enough.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Got married just before the tour. I count the days. Out loud, apparently.
? tier>=colleague
- Port Halloran rains three days in four. I moaned the whole time. I'd love a wet coat now.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The garden at misting hour. Best smell aboard. Don't tell Brennan it beats her bread.

== about
? aff:bakshi-sol:friend
- Sol misses the rain too. We stand in the garden at misting hour. Don't say anything.   #warm
? bond:friends
- {friend}. Good sort. Doesn't fuss. High praise from me.

// Writer-commons, batch 5: towards 60 (a bunkmate). Up at five for the early team; off Tue, Wed; runs the galley
// Fri, Sat. The countdown is a number said with no context.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning deck:4
- {hi}. Quiet. Tran's still asleep. She'll tell you lights out was too late.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Hm. Morning. Breakfast's on. I made it. Don't look at me like that.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}. Bar or bunk. I haven't decided. Bar.
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Still up? Me too. Night owl in an early job. Bad combination.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- You're back. Thought you'd moved bunks. Wouldn't have blamed you. Tomas hums.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {hi}. One hundred and eighty-four. Don't ask. You know.
? tier>=close
- {hi}, {nick}. Sit. I'll tell you the number. And why I like it getting smaller.   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Right. Go on.
- {bye}. Don't wake me. Up at five.
? tier>=colleague time:night
- Night. Lights out. Tran's orders. I just enforce them.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Glad you're in our bunk. Don't tell the others I said so.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Number's going down. Can't complain. Do anyway.   #funny
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Good day. Brennan's off, galley ran, nobody noticed. That's the job.
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Bit flat. Raining back home, they said. I'd give a lot to be cold and wet.

== near
? act:work
- Galley at five. Quiet. The best hour. Don't tell anyone it's the best hour.
? act:work weekday:fri|sat
- Brennan's day off. Everything's fine. Everything is fine. Pass me that ladle.   #funny
? act:leisure deck:3
- The bar's quiet. That's how I like it. One drink, one chat, then bed. Maybe two chats.
? deck:4 time:night
- Can't sleep. Lying there counting. Not sheep. Days.
? act:breakfast
- I don't eat breakfast. I make it. That's enough breakfast for anyone.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I skip breakfast. Six hours of cooking it and I can't face it. Fair, really.
? tier>=colleague
- Married just before the tour. Best decision. Worst timing. Both true.
? tier>=colleague
- Silva, Soto, Jovanovic and me. We compare counts. I'm not winning. Nobody's winning.
? tier>=friend
- Port Halloran's grey and wet and loud. I didn't know I'd love it till I left.
? tier>=friend
- They write every week. Short letters. I read them twice. Then once more in the morning.   #warm

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Misting hour. Close your eyes. That's rain on Port Halloran. Near enough.

== invite
? tier>=colleague time:afternoon
- Garden at misting hour? Five minutes. No talking. Best five minutes of the day.
? tier>=friend time:evening
- Bar later? I'll buy. One. Don't get used to it.   #funny

== accept
- Fine. I'll be there.
- Go on then. I'll bring the number.   #funny

== decline
- Can't. Up at five. Ask me on a Tuesday.
- Not tonight. Writing home. It's the long letter week.

== missed
- You didn't turn up. That's fine. I counted the days instead.   #funny
- Missed you. No bother. There's always tomorrow. Well. Fewer tomorrows. Good ones.

== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. That's one more day closer. Best present there is.   #warm
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. Saved you something from the galley. Don't ask what. Just eat it.   #warm

== hint
- Got a minute? Not here. Garden.

== week1
? week1:true weekday:mon time:morning tier<=acquaintance
- You're the new one. Bottom bunk by the wall's me. I'm up at five. Sorry in advance.
? week1:true time:night tier<=acquaintance
- Settling in? The pipes knock at two. That's normal. Go back to sleep.

== near
? act:dinner
- Eat. It's good tonight. I didn't make it. That's not why it's good. Probably.   #funny
? deck:3 act:leisure time:evening
- Same stool every night. Same drink. That's home, a bit.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance weekday:tue|wed
- {hi}. Day off. I'm going to do nothing, very slowly.
? tier>=friend
- There you are, {nick}. Saved you the good chair. Nobody fought me for it. Shame.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Brennan trusts me with her galley two days a week. I try not to let it go to my head.
? tier>=colleague
- Varga thinks we're racing at onions. We are. He's winning. Don't tell him I know.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Two hundred and six.   #funny
- Runs itself, this galley.   #funny
- Typical.
- Rain on the vents. No. Just vents.
? act:work
- Onions. Thirty-nine. Close.

== rumour
- Fact. Not gossip. Fact.
- Heard it. Probably true. Typical.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it. Quick. Thanks. That's all. Thanks.   #warm
? told:fav.job
- You did my job. Saved me an hour. I spent it sitting down. Thanks.   #funny
? told:fixed.chiller
- Chiller's fixed. Brennan smiled at the cold store. First time in weeks.   #funny
? told:came.harvest
- You came to the harvest. Carried a basket. Didn't drop it. Good.   #funny
? told:gift.garden
- From the garden. Smells like rain. Nearly. Thanks, {nick}.   #warm
? told:bday
- My birthday. You noticed. One less day. In a good way.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- Galley rates you. Brennan, Walsh, me. Three votes. That's all of them that count.   #funny
? rep:theirs
- You're galley. Officially. Don't let it go to your head. Let it go to your stomach.   #funny
? you:reliable
- Reliable. That's the word about you. Good word. Rare word.

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:garden
- From the garden. Smells green. Thanks, {nick}. That's a good one.   #warm
? gift:loved
- That's a good one. Really good. Thanks. I mean it.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thanks. Nice. Kind.
? gift:polite
- Huh. Thanks. Typical you. Kind about it.
